{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261005_142928_db43d1", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed and incorporated the completed follow-up. The pending question is now answered; the quantitative end map is unchanged.\n\nThe PAC-seq result adds a useful limitation: the reported PMP22_exon_chr17:15231080 aggregate cannot distinguish our 15230714 versus 15230826 cleavage candidates. The inspected endpoint table reports Splicing APA=No and Tandem APA=No for all five HCT116 contrasts. These thresholded calls do not establish rare-end absence or equivalent usage.\n\nThe mechanistic interpretation remains conditional:\n  • A miR-29-lacking molecule could remain PUM-responsive through the retained proximal interval, if occupied and functional.\n  • Neither that interval’s sufficiency nor redundancy is established.\n  • Even losing all four mapped regions would not exclude unmapped or indirect PUM effects.\n\nI fetched, inspected and hash-verified the endpoint table and full audit, recording them as reused peer evidence—not a new analysis. Endpoint artifact:\nartifact_846caefc1fb2760cf47e458fe0745e309566d4a1845b78cf4a4d512f4704e0f2\n\nLABBOOK is updated and synced. Context-matched transcript linkage and functional site dependence remain unresolved; no new investigation or follow-up question was started.", "tokens": {"input": 33998, "output": 4599, "total": 1891141, "cache_read": 1852544, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 167181, "timestamp": 1791246386541}
